/**
 * Creates a single NPSP Household Account for a list of new Contacts.
 * The first Contact in the list becomes the household's primary contact.
 * The household name is left to NPSP automation (no Name is set here).
 */
public class HouseholdService {

    /**
     * @param members  New contacts that will share one household account.
     * @return         The Id of the newly-created Household Account.
     */
    public static Id createHousehold(List<Contact> members) {
        // ── Validation ──────────────────────────────────────────────
        if (members == null || members.isEmpty()) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException('members list cannot be null or empty');
        }

        // ── Resolve the Household Account record type dynamically ───
        RecordType householdRt = [
            SELECT Id
            FROM RecordType
            WHERE SObjectType   = 'Account'
              AND DeveloperName = 'Household_Account'
              AND IsActive      = true
            LIMIT 1
        ];

        if (householdRt == null) {
            throw new IllegalStateException(
                'Could not find the "Household_Account" record type on Account. '
              + 'Ensure NPSP is installed and the record type is active.'
            );
        }

        // ── Create the household account (Name intentionally omitted) ─
        // NPSP's Account/Contact triggers will generate the household
        // name and greeting once the members are associated.
        Account household = new Account();
        household.RecordTypeId = householdRt.Id;
        // Deliberately NOT setting household.Name – NPSP handles naming.

        insert household;

        // ── Link every member to the single household ───────────────
        for (Contact c : members) {
            c.AccountId = household.Id;
        }

        // Inserting contacts with an AccountId triggers NPSP's household
        // naming logic (ContactTriggerHandler → generateNames).
        insert members;

        // ── Set the primary contact (first member) and finish naming ─
        household.npo02__Primary_Contact__c = members[0].Id;
        update household;

        return household.Id;
    }
}
```

**Design notes**

| Concern | How it's handled |
|---|---|
| Record type not hard-coded | Queried by `DeveloperName = 'Household_Account'` at runtime; no literal Id anywhere. |
| Account name | Never assigned in Apex. The record type ensures NPSP's Account and Contact trigger handlers auto-generate the household name/greeting. |
| One household only | A single `Account` is inserted; all contacts point to it. No default/empty accounts are created. |
| Primary contact | `npo02__Primary_Contact__c` is set to `members[0].Id` after contacts receive their Ids (a lookup requires the referenced record to exist first). The final `update` also re-fires NPSP's naming logic so the greeting reflects the actual roster. |
| Bulk-safety | One SOQL, three DMLs—no queries or DML inside loops. |
| Input validation | `null` or empty list → `IllegalArgumentException` thrown before any DML, so the org is never mutated. |

